WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.063
Abdominal illness can look similar across immune, inflammatory

00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:09.576
and infectious processes. Clinical appearance alone may be insufficient.

00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:18.873
Diagnostic interpretation can involve biomarkers, endoscopy and tissue

00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:23.863
findings, with different roles and limitations in distinct diseases.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:33.387
Part Two surveys emerging diagnostic techniques and treatments

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:38.265
for autoimmune gastrointestinal conditions in a changing evidence landscape.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:47.260
Therapeutic approaches follow disease mechanisms, but treatment evidence

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.679
differs by condition, study design and patient population.

00:00:55.883 --> 00:01:00.006
A new assay or biologic may improve the

00:01:00.006 --> 00:01:04.129
available choices without solving every diagnostic or therapeutic question.

00:01:08.092 --> 00:01:13.761
The 2022 chapter documents the literature available then. Current

00:01:13.761 --> 00:01:19.431
medical decisions require updated clinical evidence and professional evaluation.
